      <h1 class="page-title mt-4">The sign stayed up</h1>
      <div class="body-copy mt-7 space-y-5 text-[1.0625rem]">
        <p>Halina Nowak ran a lunch counter on this corner from 1961 to 2009. She made the pierogi, she knew your stool, and the sign over the door said HALINA&rsquo;S LUNCH in cream on turquoise enamel.</p>
        <p>Then the building stood empty for twelve years. The sign stayed up.</p>
        <p>Marisol Ortega ate at that counter after Mass as a child, four blocks from home. In 2021 she and Pete Kowalski bought the building with the counter, the fourteen stools and the sign still in it. They reopened in 2022, put eight booths along the windows, and started serving supper.</p>
